---
// Why we build it: the current words and the real PNAS numbers, restyled to the product page.
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { STUDY } from "../data/content";
---
<section class="sect why dark" id="why" data-bg="emerald" data-fg="dark-text" aria-labelledby="why-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center rise">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why we’re building it</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="why-h"><span class="why__dim">Most AI tools think for you.</span> <span translate="no">Neuroditto</span> helps you <em>think for yourself.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <dl class="why__grid">
      <div class="stat rise">
        <dt class="stat__label">Students in the study</dt>
        <dd class="stat__num"><small>about</small><span aria-hidden="true" data-count="1000">1,000</span><span class="visually-hidden">1,000</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="stat rise">
        <dt class="stat__label">Lower scores once answer-giving AI was taken away</dt>
        <dd class="stat__num"><span aria-hidden="true" data-count="17" data-suffix="%">17%</span><span class="visually-hidden">17%</span></dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="why__body rise">In a study of about 1,000 students, AI that gave answers made students score 17% worse once it was taken away. The same AI, built to give hints, largely avoided that drop. AI isn’t the problem. How it’s built is.</p>
    <p class="why__src rise">
      <a href={STUDY.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{STUDY.cite}<Icon name="external-link" size={16} /><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .why__dim { color: var(--c-dark-text-2); }
  .why__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .stat {
    background: var(--c-dark-card); border-radius: 28px; padding: 30px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-dark-text) 6%, transparent);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  /* Sized to its own card: "1,000" in Syne 800 is about 4.2em wide, so 22cqi always fits. */
  .stat__num { order: 1; font: 800 min(clamp(64px, 8vw, 112px), 22cqi)/.85 var(--font-accent); color: var(--c-light-gold); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin-left: -.04em; }
  .stat__num small { display: block; font: 500 var(--fs-lead)/1.2 var(--font-sans); color: var(--c-dark-text-2); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .stat__label { order: 2; color: var(--c-dark-text-2); max-width: 30ch; }
  .why__body { color: var(--c-dark-text-2); font-size: var(--fs-lead); max-width: 54ch; margin: 36px auto 0; text-align: center; }
  .why__src { text-align: center; margin-top: 20px; }
  .why__src a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; min-height: 44px; color: var(--c-light-gold); font-size: var(--fs-small); font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .why__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
